Tag name: cam6_2_037
Originator(s): cjablono, pel, eaton
Date: Mon Jul 20 15:02:31 MDT 2020
One-line Summary: fixes for simple models; fixes for SE/WACCM-X
Github PR URL: https://github.com/ESCOMP/CAM/pull/168

Purpose of changes (include the issue number and title text for each relevant GitHub issue):

Fixes issue #143 Changes for Simple Models from Christiane
Fixes issue #158 Update tag used for atmospheric_physics
Fixes issue #170 fixes for SE/WACCM-X

. The existing logic allows the dycore initialization to adjust the
  atmosphere dry mass when simple physics is used with initial conditions
  read from a file (rather than being analytic).  Modify EUL, FV, and SE
  dycores so the initialization does not change the dry mass of the
  atmosphere for simple physics configurations.

. Modify EUL to not hardcode the dry mass for Held-Suarez.  This allows
  Held-Suarez configurations with topography as allowed by FV and SE.

. Modify EUL to avoid the application of the energy fixer in case of
  tj2016_phys.

. Update the NCAR/atmospheric_physics external to get fixes to kessler:
  - fix relative humidity diagnostics with unphysical large values (> 100%)
  - fix time step subcycling algorithm
  - fix physical constants

. The initialization of constituents was recently refactored to allow
  reading constituent fields (except Q) from an initial file even when the
  analytic IC option was used.  A problem arose with the FKESSLER compset
  because the initial file was from a cam5 simulation and contained the
  CLDLIQ field which overwrote the analytic IC specification for CLDLIQ.
  The code has been modified so that no water species is read from the
  initial file when the analytic IC option is in use.

. Bug fixes for SE/WACCM-X (issue #170)

Describe any changes made to build system: none

