Tag name: cam6_2_031
Originator(s): fvitt, aherring
Date: 9 Jun 2020
One-line Summary: Aerosol convection processes; ChangeLog template update
Github PR URL: https://github.com/ESCOMP/CAM/pull/149

Purpose of changes (include the issue number and title text for each relevant GitHub issue):

. Refactor how resuspension of aerosols from rain to coarse modes is done in aerosol convective
  processes.  This fixes GitHub issue "Bug in aerosol wet removal" #140.

. Improvement of vertical velocity calculation in aerosol deep convction processes through
  backing out the vertical velocities from zm mass fluxes using an assumed convective area
  fraction of 0.01. This value was found to give the appropriate magnitude of vertical
  velocities in the GATEIII iop, using the single column model (aherring)

. Update ChangeLog template to replace Bugzilla with Github #152

Describe any changes made to build system:

Describe any changes made to the namelist:

List any changes to the defaults for the boundary datasets:

Describe any substantial timing or memory changes:

Code reviewed by:

List all files eliminated:

List all files added and what they do:

List all existing files that have been modified, and describe the changes:

src/chemistry/modal_aero/modal_aero_convproc.F90
 - Refactor how resuspension of aerosols from rain to coarse modes is done
 - Improve the calculation of vertical velocities in aerosol deep convection
   processes through backing out the vertical velocities from zm mass fluxes
   using an assumed convective area fraction of 0.01. This value was found to
   give the appropriate magnitude of vertical velocities in the GATEIII iop,
   using the single column model. (aherring)
 - Misc code cleanup

src/chemistry/modal_aero/modal_aero_data.F90
 - determine the order (largest to smallest) mode sizes

cime_config/testdefs/testlist_cam.xml
 - move the "wetdep" to the "camchem" suite

doc/ChangeLog_template
 - reference github issue titles and numbers (rather than bugzilla ID)

