    - less than 200 m changes to CONUS, ARCTIC & ARCTICGRIS topography,
    - minor regional impacts on the climate,

    - changes to F/B compset ncdata files for ne30.xx, ne120.xx, CONUS, ARCTIC & ARCTICGRIS,
    - only impacts the spin-up adjustment in ne30.xx / ne120.xx due to more consistent inic
    - No change in climate for all cases

    - new clubb_gamma and clubb_c14 values significantly change the climate,
    - the lower values increase SWCF and bring RESTOM closer to 0

    - setting clubb time-steps for CONUS, ARCTIC & ARCTICGRIS that makes explicit time-steps used in the model,
    - BFB since this does not change the clubb time-step

    - setting hyper-viscosity on temperature equal to that on pressure, and
    - increasing nu does not noticeably impact climate.
    - intention of these changes are to stabilizes the dycore for deacadal and longer runs

    - increase se_nu_top to tune the polar night jets and reduce cold pole bias,
    - so it does impact high altitude climate

