Tag name: cam6_2_004
Originator(s): fvitt
Date: 30 Oct 2019
One-line Summary: Use Heelis high-latitude electric potential model in WACCM

Purpose of changes:

WACCM has been using the empirical Weimer96 high-latitude electric potential model
while WACCMX defaults to the Heelis empirical model and has the option to use Weimer05
(WACCMX does not use Weimer96).  The change here removes the deprecated Weimer96 module
from WACCM physics.  The parameterization of the electric potential and electric fields
used to derive ion drift velocities and joule heating in WACCM will use the Heelis
empirical model over the polar cap regions.  This will be more consistent with the
default WACCMX configuration.

Bugs fixed (include bugzilla ID):

Describe any changes made to build system:

Describe any changes made to the namelist:

List any changes to the defaults for the boundary datasets:

Describe any substantial timing or memory changes:

