One-line Summary: Misc WACCM(X) updates and bug fixes

Purpose of changes:

 Add support for 2-degrees FWmaSD and FC6XSD compsets

 Correct "-chem" configure option in CAM_CONFIG_OPTS for FXmad* compsets
  -- the 'additive' modifier for CAM_CONFIG_OPTS caused the setting to be
     "-chem waccm_ma -chem waccm_mad" for CAM40%WXIED (WACCM-X with
     D-region chemistry).  The change here distinguishes "CAM40%WXIE" from
     "CAM40%WXIED" so that only waccm_mad is selected for CAM40%WXIED.

 Zero the energetic particle forcings beyond the vertical extent of the input data
  -- energetic particle forcings during large solar events were producing unrealistic
     amounts of N(2D) near the top of WACCMX due to the ion production rates above
     the top of input files were set to the values at the top of the input data.
     Zeroing the production rates above the input files corrects this problem.

 Adjust Nitric Oxide deactivation rate (in NO cooling) to be consistent with
 TIEGCM (Hwang et al., 2003)

Bugs fixed (include bugzilla ID):

Describe any changes made to build system:

Describe any changes made to the namelist:

