One-line Summary: cleanup in diagnostic output and simple model code

Purpose of changes:

. Use the cam_export routine to set the psl component of CAM's export
  object.  Use the pbuf to communicate PSL.

. Cleanup use of CAM data structures in the simple model control and CAM
  interface layers.  Move towards being consistent with architecture of
  full physics code.

Bugs fixed (include bugzilla ID): none

Describe any changes made to build system: none

Describe any changes made to the namelist: none

List any changes to the defaults for the boundary datasets: none

Describe any substantial timing or memory changes: none

Code reviewed by: eaton

List all files eliminated: none

List all files added and what they do: none

List all existing files that have been modified, and describe the changes:

components/cam/bld/namelist_files/namelist_definition.xml
. add 'nhours' as valid value for stop_option

components/cam/bld/namelist_files/use_cases/dctest_tj2016.xml
. add VT,UU,VV,VU to fincl1

components/cam/src/control/camsrfexch.F90
. set the psl component of the export state from PSL field in pbuf.

components/cam/src/physics/cam/cam_diagnostics.F90
. add PSL to pbuf
. diag_phys_writeout_dry
  - set psl in pbuf rather than passing it as an intent(out) arg.
. diag_phys_writeout
  - remove psl as an optional arg and add pbuf as required arg.

components/cam/src/physics/cam/physpkg.F90
. in tphysbc fix actual args in diag_phys_writeout call

components/cam/src/physics/simple/kessler_cam.F90
. have this module manage the PREC_SED pbuf field rather than having
  it done in the tphysbc control layer.
. change the exner calc to use a local variable rather than setting the
  component in the state object in a manner incompatible with how it's set
  in dp_coupling.
. remove setting of precl in the export state object.  now done by
  cam_export routine analogously to full physics

components/cam/src/physics/simple/physpkg.F90
. remove adding PREC_SED to pbuf.  belongs in kesser interface
. tphysac
  - add call to diag_surf.  This provides outfld calls for components of
    CAM's import state.  The sequencing is different than in the full
    physics code to allow the simple models to provide the surface forcings
    rather than assuming they come from the surface component models.
. tphysbc
  - update actual args in call to kessler_tend and diag_phys_writeout
  - remove moist_physics conditional from calls to diag_phys_writeout and
    diag_conv as in full physics version.  The moist_physics condition is
    addressed internally in these routines.
  - add call to cam_export which is responsible for setting the components
    of the export state object.

components/cam/src/physics/simple/tj2016_cam.F90
. thatcher_jablonowski_sfc_pbl_hs_tend
  - set the components of the import state that are diagnosed in this
    routine.
  - remove outfld calls for the surface forcing fields.  They have been put
    in the import state object and the outfld calls are provided by the
    call to diag_surf added to tphysac.

components/cam/src/physics/spcam/spcam_drivers.F90
. fix interface of diag_phys_writeout


