Tag name: cam5_4_165
Originator(s): fvitt
Date: 8 Feb 2018
One-line Summary: Corrections to WACCM solar forcings

Purpose of changes:

 - Use time_coordinate utility class in epp_ionization module to manage time interpolations
   -- this corrects the timing of energetic particle forcings (leap day issue)
 - Vertically interpolate ionization rates over log pressure rather than pressure
 - Implement capability in time_coordinate utility to time-interpolate to some delta-time
   which is not current model time, such as delta_days=-1 for the previous day (24 hrs prior)
 - Pass in previous day's F10.7cm radio flux scaled by earth-sun distance factor to MSIS
   for WACCM upper boundary (time interpolated to 24 hours prior to the current model time)
 - Time-interpolate WACCM "solar parms" input data (space weather indices Kp, F10.7, Ap)
   -- these had been held constant between data times
 - Use corrected solar forcing files in WACCM compsets
 - Add "f107p" to CAM history files (previous day's F10.7cm radio flux)


Bugs fixed (include bugzilla ID):
 Fixes an issue with the timing of solar proton events when the model calendar is
 set to noleap and the ionization input file includes leap days.

